WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.540
- [Spider-Man] You have a
knack for getting in trouble.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.060
- You have a knack for saving my life.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.420
(upbeat orchestral music)

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.160
- [Sam Raimi] For me it
was a great love story,

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.840
with a real human being at the center,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.520
somebody I could really identify with.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.880
Somebody who had to do homework,

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.020
someone who the girls weren't crazy about,

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.020
somebody who was bullied.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.420
And yet he had to rise
up and become this hero

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.440
to protect the city.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.680
And it seemed like they had
never heard that version before.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.240
I had great graphic images,
of how Spider-Man lands,

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.080
what his pose looks like,
how he swings from a web.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.480
The job was to bring that
vision to the big screen.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.360
How would we do that?

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.840
How would we get actors to move in a way

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.360
that only a comic book
artist could depict?

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.940
That was really the challenge.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.320
- [Jeff] The mandate was just

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.340
to make it as real as we could.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.880
When Toby's hanging upside
down, in the pouring rain,

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.200
and she's all wet.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:57.860
- [Sam] This was the
moment when Peter debugged

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.380
that she's his dream, of
helping the woman he loved.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.320
It's also of finally getting
to kiss the woman he loved.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.600
The vulnerability that he exposes to her.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.720
I think that's why her
pulling down the mask makes

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.620
the moment special,
because his character longs

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.000
to be loved by her.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.440
And to remove the mask
is exposing yourself

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.620
to becoming vulnerable
with someone who loves you.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.360
- [Jeff] There was a considerable
amount of setup time.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.540
We were actually outside on the backlot

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.920
with big rain machines but to
be able to see rain in movies

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.920
it actually has to be a lot
bigger drops than real life rain

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.880
so when you're getting
rained on in the movies,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.180
it's a lot of water.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.240
- [Sam] You do take after
take and they're being doused

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:36.060
in cold water and it can
become really chilling.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.600
- [Jeff] But we would have to
get out there, get in position

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.020
and get the rain going,
and then we would have

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.660
to lift Toby up on the wire, upside down,

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.320
in the position you saw him in the movie,

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:46.860
and that would take a couple minutes,

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:50.440
so it's a few minutes of misery
each time we do the take.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.560
- [Sam] And while he was
doing the scene I remember

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.200
the water was falling down

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.740
into his upside down nostrils,

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.340
so he was kind of drowning
but it was a kissing scene

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.560
so (laughs) he had to pretend, like,

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.720
it was a pleasant, sweet moment for him,

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:02.960
when in fact he was semi-drowning,

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.940
and then the only way he could
breathe was through his mouth

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.640
and then I had him kiss Kirsten.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.220
They seemed to do very well with it.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.220
It was more about trickery
of the mask itself.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.540
We couldn't really get
that look on the mask

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.440
and have it be pliable, so
it really wouldn't pull up

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.980
and down, and we had to
pretend as though it were.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.040
But Kirsten's doing a little
bit of sleight of hand

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.760
that helps sell the idea
that she actually pulled

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:23.700
the mask down.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.720
It was a lot of technical
aspects but fortunately Kirsten

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.140
and Toby are so convincing that

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.900
they made that all invisible.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.100
- [Jeff] I felt the pressure
that the genre was in trouble.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.840
Hollywood was soured on the
superhero film around 1999.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.640
I honestly in my heart
think that this movie

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.760
and how Sam did it absolutely
set the tone of how

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.000
a comic book movie should be made.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.840
- [Sam] I love Stan Lee's
work and I was trying

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.500
to be true to it, and if
people recognize from those

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:51.180
Spider-Man movies that his
stories were really effective,

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.100
then I'm proud.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.660
(dramatic music)

